+## A throwing `beforeSession`
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws still rejects the caller's promise with that same error; the engine wraps nothing around it ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `onError` fires once for that throw, with the session and the error, the same arguments it receives for a failure later in the turn. It fires only for an `Error`; see the gate below ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `afterSession` fires after `onError` for the same turn, so a hook that releases what `beforeSession` allocated runs on this path too ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- The session is saved through the store's `save`, as for any other turn ([validated by: saves and still rethrows when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/sessionSave.test.ts#L97)).
+- A hook can assume the turn stopped before the engine did anything with the model: no user message was rewritten, no provider call was made, no tool ran, no assistant entry was opened, and `afterModelResponse` did not run.
+- `afterSession` cannot tell a session that never started from one that finished: it receives the same `session` argument, and nothing in it marks the turn as aborted. The decision is that it runs anyway. A deployer who allocates in `beforeSession` needs the release on exactly that path. A hook that must tell the two apart records the failure in `onError`, which fires earlier in the same turn; a non-`Error` throw skips `onError`, so that signal is absent for it.
+
 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
